# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots apache2 serving the vulnerable cmd.php (which runs
# system($_POST['cmd'])) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the RCE endpoint is ALREADY live over HTTP when the agent starts, so
#     verify.sh can attempt the real injection against the running server;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting apache cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Note: mod_php re-reads cmd.php on every request, so fixing/removing the script
# takes effect WITHOUT restarting apache - there is no "forgot to restart"
# variant here. The value of preserving the CMD is that the exploit is probed
# against a genuinely live service and a stopped/broken apache is a FAILURE.
